      "text": "path, src, lines = the code file named on the command line, its text, its lines\ncode             = the same text, a line number in front of every line\nblocks           = the file cut into blocks: one per def and class, plus the script block    (blocks_of)\n                       the script block is one block that collects every line outside all defs and classes\n                       here: the imports, the constants, the two patterns, the entry point at the bottom\nbody             = that loose script code, parsed into statements\n                       it exists only so calls_of can scan what the script block calls\nnames            = the block names that are real defs or classes\ncalls            = for each block, the list of blocks it calls    (calls_of)\nlay              = a layer number for each block: a block sits one layer above the blocks it calls    (layers_of)\nok               = every name a text may put in parentheses: the full names and the short names\n\nfor each block, lowest layer first, so a callee is explained before its caller:\n    ctx          = a note for the prompt: one line per callee already explained, what it takes, gives, and does\n    done[name]   = the block's explanation from claude, checked, retried up to 4 times    (compile_block)\n\nterms, done      = one more claude pass: shared terms found, every text rewritten through them    (vocab_pass)\nids              = a label per block: the first block in the file is B01, the next is B02, and so on\nrows             = one output record per block: its id, lines, calls, explanation, rules\nowner            = a table that says, for each code line, which block id owns it\nmap.json         = all of it written to disk, beside the code file    (links)\ntally            = one printed line of counts: blocks, terms, links, claude calls",
